WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.000
[theme song playing]

00:17.680 --> 00:21.320
♪ Take a little walk
To the edge of town ♪

00:21.400 --> 00:23.600
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

00:25.560 --> 00:27.920
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

00:28.000 --> 00:29.520
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

00:29.600 --> 00:34.000
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

00:34.080 --> 00:38.240
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

00:38.320 --> 00:40.080
♪ In the humming wires ♪

00:40.160 --> 00:41.120
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

00:41.200 --> 00:43.440
♪ You're never coming back ♪

00:43.520 --> 00:45.640
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

00:45.720 --> 00:47.960
♪ Past the mills
Past the stacks ♪

00:50.600 --> 00:53.000
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

00:53.080 --> 00:54.760
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

00:54.840 --> 00:57.040
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

00:57.120 --> 00:59.040
♪ A red right hand ♪

01:10.800 --> 01:12.640
[Nutley] Your brothers came to my house.

01:14.000 --> 01:16.880
They said the Peaky Blinders
had business with me.

01:18.960 --> 01:20.120
[Tommy] You're not afraid of me.

01:29.440 --> 01:30.440
So,

01:31.240 --> 01:33.640
what is it you want
from a simple working man?

01:34.480 --> 01:35.560
Fear.

01:36.680 --> 01:38.000
[thunder rumbling]

01:40.680 --> 01:42.840
Poor Mr. Nutley drank too much.

01:44.400 --> 01:48.080
He went for a piss on the train tracks
that run behind the factory.

01:48.800 --> 01:50.040
Train came.

01:52.160 --> 01:54.440
They found his body in Saltley
broken into bits.

01:54.560 --> 01:56.120
I know what you do.

01:57.160 --> 01:58.560
Tell me what you want.

02:04.360 --> 02:05.280
There.

02:06.240 --> 02:10.120
The lot's complete warehouse.
Bays four, five and six.

02:10.320 --> 02:11.600
You have the keys?

02:11.880 --> 02:13.600
Yes, I have keys.

02:14.800 --> 02:16.240
What's in bay four?

02:17.320 --> 02:20.720
Completed type 40s and type 21s
waiting for the paint shop.

02:21.560 --> 02:22.800
Bay five?

02:23.240 --> 02:25.400
-[Nutley] Paint shop and parts.
-Uh-huh.

02:26.680 --> 02:27.840
So, it's bay six.

02:28.440 --> 02:29.600
What is?

02:30.560 --> 02:31.720
[inhales sharply]

02:31.800 --> 02:33.680
Give me the keys to bay six.

02:35.360 --> 02:37.000
It's just old stock in storage.

02:37.960 --> 02:40.120
Give me the keys to bay six.

02:42.160 --> 02:43.720
[sighs]

02:54.160 --> 02:55.680
[keys jangling]

03:07.320 --> 03:08.520
For your trouble.

03:09.640 --> 03:11.080
Give it to your charity.

03:20.200 --> 03:22.800
I'm only doing this
for the safety of my family.

03:27.320 --> 03:29.320
[rock music playing]

04:07.120 --> 04:08.160
[grunts]

04:26.840 --> 04:28.160
[sighs]

04:28.240 --> 04:29.320
[sniffs]

04:47.280 --> 04:48.360
[sighs]

04:48.880 --> 04:53.240
[Hughes] So, will it be just boys in your
charitable institution or girls as well?

04:55.320 --> 04:56.640
Both.

04:57.800 --> 04:59.080
You must divide them.

05:00.080 --> 05:02.200
You know how the little creatures can get.

05:04.280 --> 05:07.120
Where are your people?
You said they'd be here by 5:00.

05:07.960 --> 05:09.560
[Hughes] They are a law unto themselves.

05:10.200 --> 05:12.560
You can never quite grasp who they are.

05:13.400 --> 05:14.960
Like gripping wet soap.

05:17.200 --> 05:18.920
I've done my research.

05:19.400 --> 05:21.440
[Hughes mutters]

05:21.960 --> 05:25.920
Perhaps you know them
as the, uh, Economic League.

05:26.800 --> 05:30.160
Only once did I get a letter from them
headed "The Vigilance Committee."

05:30.360 --> 05:32.080
Which tips the hand a little.

05:32.360 --> 05:34.160
[clicks tongue] No.

05:34.520 --> 05:37.320
The name I've heard is Section D.

05:37.600 --> 05:40.320
-[pouring drink]
-That's what Special Branch calls them.

05:41.080 --> 05:44.840
Businessmen, MPs, army officers.

05:46.640 --> 05:47.920
[exhales]

05:48.920 --> 05:52.200
[Hughes] Yes, it will be fun to bring
such men to a Gypsy scrapyard.

05:52.280 --> 05:53.520
[scoffs]

05:55.240 --> 05:56.800
You asked for privacy.

05:57.240 --> 06:01.440
Since the election, the government
has decided that we are the enemy.

06:02.680 --> 06:06.040
When all we're trying to do
is save the country from revolution.

06:08.240 --> 06:10.640
Are you political, Mr. Shelby?

06:12.040 --> 06:13.360
Because these Odd Fellows believe

06:13.440 --> 06:16.960
that the time is coming soon
when everyone must choose a side.

06:19.120 --> 06:21.400
Are your people coming
or are they not coming?

06:22.040 --> 06:25.240
Mr. Shelby, you will learn that
these men are far too grand

06:25.320 --> 06:27.040
for the clock to govern them.

06:28.600 --> 06:31.680
You'll get used to meeting
in the small hours of the morning.

06:32.440 --> 06:33.480
They're like monks.

06:37.160 --> 06:39.880
So, when is your
charitable institute opening?

06:40.240 --> 06:42.080
[exhales] When I fucking say.

06:44.120 --> 06:47.000
Well, I'll stop by from time to time

06:47.080 --> 06:49.400
to hear confession
from the little creatures.

06:51.240 --> 06:53.920
You'll meet Mr. Patrick Jarvis, MP.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.040
He'll probably want to become a trustee.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.720
It's just his thing, to drop by
in the evenings after a few drinks.

07:01.640 --> 07:06.200
We'll make it a formal arrangement
as part of the bigger deal between us.

07:08.120 --> 07:10.560
-I will have an office there.
-[clearing throat]

07:13.120 --> 07:14.640
[Tommy sniffles]

07:15.760 --> 07:16.920
[spits]

07:17.760 --> 07:18.760
Ah!

07:20.040 --> 07:22.760
My God.
Some devil gets into you, doesn't it, boy?

07:25.440 --> 07:27.080
Mr. Shelby,

07:27.640 --> 07:32.640
if I want to play the squire in
your place of false charity, then I will.

07:33.680 --> 07:36.880
Ambition for respectability
doesn't make you a saint.

07:37.480 --> 07:38.680
Am I wrong?

07:40.480 --> 07:42.200
[bell tolling]

07:43.640 --> 07:45.480
Oh, Lord. That's 6:00, is it?

07:47.520 --> 07:50.160
Well, I wish you a good day.

07:50.960 --> 07:52.440
Where the fuck are you going?

07:52.520 --> 07:54.080
Did I not make it clear?

07:54.880 --> 07:57.200
They said if they weren't here
by morning prayers

07:57.280 --> 07:59.080
then the meeting has been canceled.

08:00.400 --> 08:04.120
Perhaps Mr. Jarvis has been held up
at the House of Commons.

08:05.040 --> 08:08.080
Perhaps Admiral Hall's been held up
at the House of Lords.

08:09.200 --> 08:10.560
Am I impressing you?

08:11.720 --> 08:14.480
Or perhaps they have decided
they don't care for doing business

08:14.560 --> 08:16.720
with Gypsies in scrap metal yards

08:17.120 --> 08:19.360
which would be a poor outcome for you.

08:19.440 --> 08:21.960
You give them my message from me, Priest.

08:24.040 --> 08:26.520
You tell them I've been to the factories

08:26.920 --> 08:29.440
and the armored vehicles
are in good condition.

08:32.039 --> 08:33.440
[Hughes] How many?

08:35.400 --> 08:36.840
Twenty-seven.

08:37.720 --> 08:39.559
And the foreman is ours.

08:42.000 --> 08:43.799
This is someone you'll meet.

08:44.440 --> 08:46.240
Today, at the Ritz.

08:46.920 --> 08:48.280
I have meetings today.

08:48.800 --> 08:51.440
You have one meeting, this one.

08:52.240 --> 08:53.480
In London.

08:54.880 --> 08:56.760
So, you'd best catch the milk train.

09:04.120 --> 09:06.040
[violin playing]

09:08.280 --> 09:10.160
[birds chirping]

09:55.880 --> 09:56.840
Cold.

09:57.360 --> 09:58.280
My apologies, sir.

09:58.600 --> 10:00.400
And how many times
I asked you to tell them

10:00.480 --> 10:02.280
about sending us the servant's crockery.

10:02.360 --> 10:04.720
[butler] I have no control
over the choice of service, sir.

10:04.800 --> 10:08.360
Hmm, and what about yesterday's eggs
and last year's fish

10:08.760 --> 10:11.040
and last century's tea leaves
in a cracked pot.

10:11.160 --> 10:14.720
Sir, I have a list of today's social
engagements, if you'd like to hear them.

10:14.800 --> 10:16.080
Oh, are we in a rush today?

10:16.200 --> 10:17.960
-I have duties at the main house, sir.
-Mmm.

10:19.240 --> 10:22.320
[butler] Luncheon at The Ritz
with Duke Michail Michailovich.

10:22.400 --> 10:23.640
[Leon, in Russian]
He is such a bore.

10:23.720 --> 10:25.040
Canceled.

10:25.520 --> 10:29.160
-[in English] What reason?
-[butler] He says he is unwell, sir.

10:31.160 --> 10:33.640
You are due to have tea at 3:00

10:33.720 --> 10:37.600
with Prince Sevlod Ianovich
and Lady Mary Lewington, sir.

10:38.920 --> 10:41.200
Mmm! Good.

10:41.320 --> 10:43.880
I miss out on the bore
and meet the beauty.

10:44.040 --> 10:45.880
However, in the absence of the Duke,

10:46.040 --> 10:49.880
the, uh, Prince and the Lady,
too have canceled, sir.

10:53.400 --> 10:56.040
Other than that,
your day is, uh, your own.

10:57.520 --> 10:59.320
You do have one business appointment

10:59.880 --> 11:04.480
to discuss automobiles
with a Mr. Thomas Shelby, sir.

11:09.400 --> 11:10.680
[horse whinnying]

11:10.800 --> 11:12.960
["DNA" playing]

11:22.040 --> 11:26.560
♪ We will not be moved by it ♪

11:31.000 --> 11:33.680
You asked for a meeting out in the open,

11:34.480 --> 11:37.520
fresh air and the fine aroma of shit.

11:39.000 --> 11:40.280
"Neutral ground," you said.

11:41.240 --> 11:43.680
[Vicente] This is hardly neutral ground.

11:44.000 --> 11:46.880
Well, it's what you've got.

11:47.160 --> 11:49.640
So, por favor,

11:50.920 --> 11:51.840
sit down.

11:52.560 --> 11:54.360
-[Vicente] Where is Thomas?
-He got called away.

11:54.480 --> 11:55.480
He'd said he'd be here.

11:55.600 --> 11:56.600
[Arthur] Yeah, he is busy.

11:56.760 --> 11:59.080
And I just told you he got called away.
What do you want?

12:05.520 --> 12:07.600
There has been a peace

12:08.440 --> 12:12.720
between the Peaky Blinders and
the Changretta family for two years now...

12:12.880 --> 12:13.960
Do you want some tea or not?

12:15.640 --> 12:18.480
Here, Finn, pour the Italians
some English tea. Go on.

12:19.640 --> 12:21.520
We don't want fucking tea.

12:26.360 --> 12:28.120
We want an explanation.

12:28.440 --> 12:29.680
Well, I'll have fucking tea.

12:30.080 --> 12:31.800
Explanation for what?

12:32.520 --> 12:36.560
The Little Venice Restaurant
on Forge Street was burnt down...

12:36.960 --> 12:39.200
No. No. Couldn't have been us,
we was at a wedding.

12:39.360 --> 12:44.200
You burnt it down to stop my son
being at that same wedding.

12:44.640 --> 12:45.800
He wasn't missed.

12:46.040 --> 12:47.080
[laughs]

12:48.480 --> 12:49.720
[chuckles]

12:50.560 --> 12:52.360
You are such big boys now.

12:53.240 --> 12:57.040
But once you borrowed clothes from us
to look like men.

12:57.560 --> 12:59.600
-How's the tea, Arthur? Is it...
-[splashes]

13:01.720 --> 13:03.080
It's cold.

13:05.800 --> 13:07.520
Please tell Tommy

13:08.200 --> 13:10.680
that we pay him
whatever he asks us to pay.

13:10.760 --> 13:13.560
We stay out of the city
and off the tracks.

13:14.280 --> 13:17.560
But you tell him from me

13:18.640 --> 13:23.160
that my son will walk
with any woman in this city.

13:23.440 --> 13:25.000
Any woman he chooses.

13:25.480 --> 13:29.240
Even if that woman works for the emperor,
Thomas Shelby.

13:29.720 --> 13:31.360
My son is in love...

13:31.720 --> 13:32.960
[John snorts]

13:33.480 --> 13:36.040
[John chuckling] Sorry. Do excuse me.

13:36.720 --> 13:38.880
[sniffs] Carry on.

13:42.640 --> 13:47.120
[Vicente] And if he wishes,
he will walk with the woman he loves.

13:47.600 --> 13:48.600
Okay.

13:50.360 --> 13:51.560
You know...

13:52.160 --> 13:54.480
It would be hard for your son
to walk anywhere

13:55.240 --> 13:57.560
with a bullet in each knee, wouldn't it.

14:05.800 --> 14:06.880
Too much.

14:09.120 --> 14:11.320
You said too much, my friend.

14:12.280 --> 14:14.960
Sabini says, "Suck and swallow." But no.

14:16.080 --> 14:17.080
Too much.

14:18.360 --> 14:20.320
I spit. [spits]

14:20.880 --> 14:23.000
[Vicente speaking Italian]

14:26.240 --> 14:28.960
[John] Oh. Okay. A bit strong.

14:34.440 --> 14:36.920
-[laughs] Fucking hell.
-Isiah.

14:38.040 --> 14:40.720
Put two extra men on our pubs in Nechells.

14:41.400 --> 14:42.840
What are you talking about, Arthur?

14:43.080 --> 14:44.880
We're not scared of
fucking Eyeties anymore.

14:45.040 --> 14:48.280
Don't tell Tommy about the chair
and clean this fucking shit up.

14:50.000 --> 14:52.240
We're not scared of fucking wops!

14:52.400 --> 14:53.760
[grumbles] All right, John.

14:54.760 --> 14:56.080
Arthur!

15:01.440 --> 15:02.640
[Tommy] Hello, Ada.

15:05.680 --> 15:07.360
[Ada] Tommy Shelby? In a library?

15:07.440 --> 15:10.280
[Tommy] I need to borrow a book
about the Russian Revolution.

15:18.720 --> 15:20.920
[Ada] Have you got a new wharf
at Maida Vale now?

15:21.400 --> 15:23.240
[Tommy] I've got a new wharf
everywhere now.

15:23.600 --> 15:25.640
[Ada] Sometimes, I see our trucks
driving past.

15:26.320 --> 15:27.240
[Tommy] "Our" trucks?

15:28.720 --> 15:30.200
Shelby trucks.

15:30.960 --> 15:32.280
Why the interest?

15:32.880 --> 15:35.120
Eh, I just want to broaden my mind.

15:35.760 --> 15:38.440
Well, this is a list of the bastards
who ran away.

15:38.520 --> 15:42.280
And this is written from the point of view
of the peoples' struggle.

15:42.360 --> 15:43.560
Uh-huh.

15:45.600 --> 15:47.280
[Ada] There was a Russian at your wedding.

15:49.080 --> 15:51.240
He wouldn't tell me
how come he got invited.

15:54.760 --> 15:59.800
Well, sometimes,
exiled Russian aristocrats get invited

16:01.120 --> 16:03.200
to social occasions to add a bit of class.

16:03.480 --> 16:04.880
Is that why he was there?

16:06.240 --> 16:07.560
Why do you want to know?

16:08.800 --> 16:11.520
He was nice.
Maybe I'd like to see him again.

16:11.600 --> 16:13.040
Would that be possible?

16:13.920 --> 16:15.320
No. That would not be possible.

16:15.400 --> 16:17.720
What business do you have
with the Russians, Tommy?

16:20.320 --> 16:21.320
Can I rip this page out?

16:21.400 --> 16:22.880
No, you cannot rip that page out.

16:22.960 --> 16:24.320
-Property of the people.
-[sighing]

16:24.560 --> 16:26.040
Tommy, when Arthur took the Russian away,

16:26.120 --> 16:27.560
he had his killing pistol
under his jacket.

16:27.640 --> 16:29.880
And then Johnny lit a fire in the woods.

16:31.640 --> 16:34.120
You want all the details
because you're bored, Ada.

16:36.880 --> 16:39.480
You used to chase rats
with a revolver, Ada.

16:39.560 --> 16:41.440
-[people shushing]
-[softly] For fuck's sake.

16:41.600 --> 16:44.080
I might just have a job for you after all.

16:44.200 --> 16:45.280
[sighs]

16:48.320 --> 16:50.320
[rock music playing]

16:52.920 --> 16:54.960
[indistinct conversations]

17:12.119 --> 17:13.839
Did we run Kempton yesterday or not?

17:14.440 --> 17:15.839
Danny Lee got drunk.

17:16.480 --> 17:18.119
Instead of injecting the horses
with cocaine,

17:18.200 --> 17:19.680
he decided to share it with his cousins.

17:20.880 --> 17:22.800
[sighs] Jesus Christ.

17:23.040 --> 17:24.920
He's your brother-in-law.

17:25.000 --> 17:26.839
Tell Esme to speak to him about it.

17:27.359 --> 17:30.280
Look. Before I start...

17:33.240 --> 17:35.240
I don't want you to do anything
about this.

17:36.560 --> 17:37.680
About what?

17:39.920 --> 17:41.080
Vicente Changretta's son.

17:42.040 --> 17:45.120
-The one Lizzie was stepping out with--
-What, Angel?

17:45.240 --> 17:47.280
He's no bigger
than twopence worth of change.

17:47.440 --> 17:50.000
Well, he heard you threatened him
directly to shoot him in the knees.

17:50.080 --> 17:52.560
And now he's going around Nechells
telling everybody he's going to kill you.

17:54.400 --> 17:57.560
This is Lizzie's fault to start with,
Tommy's for leaving it up to you.

17:57.680 --> 17:59.040
What are you talking about?

18:00.360 --> 18:01.520
We run London.

18:02.000 --> 18:03.960
We run the north,
we run the whole fucking country.

18:04.080 --> 18:06.360
What do we care about
some fucking Nechells Green Eyeties?

18:06.440 --> 18:08.960
We don't need to be getting involved
in all these little piss pots.

18:09.280 --> 18:10.360
What does Arthur say?

18:11.440 --> 18:14.560
That's why I'm here and not him.

18:15.680 --> 18:17.440
If he said it, there'd be a fight.

18:18.280 --> 18:19.280
He says,

18:20.880 --> 18:22.040
"Apologize."

18:24.040 --> 18:25.280
[sniffs]

18:26.000 --> 18:27.640
He fucking said what?

18:28.000 --> 18:29.840
[Polly] We own the city.

18:30.280 --> 18:32.480
But we don't need to rub
everybody's noses in it.

18:32.840 --> 18:36.040
If the old man decides to make a stand,
he might get Sabini feeling sentimental...

18:36.120 --> 18:37.640
[John] Sabini's done.

18:41.440 --> 18:42.840
They're all done.

18:44.160 --> 18:46.080
And they all pay up.

18:47.520 --> 18:51.480
But we don't want rebellions.

18:51.760 --> 18:52.880
[sighs]

18:53.800 --> 18:56.200
What does, um, Tommy say?

18:56.480 --> 18:58.680
Tommy's busy. He left me in charge.

18:59.160 --> 19:00.400
And what do you say?

19:04.960 --> 19:06.800
-Compromise.
-Mmm-hmm.

19:08.360 --> 19:09.920
I've asked Lizzie to do it for you.

19:10.360 --> 19:12.720
She's going to meet him,
break up with him for good,

19:12.800 --> 19:15.280
apologize for any inconvenience,
say it was all her fault...

19:15.360 --> 19:16.680
-For fuck's sake!
-[clattering]

19:18.640 --> 19:20.200
[hesitates] You know what all this is?

19:20.400 --> 19:22.080
This is Arthur's fucking missus.

19:22.520 --> 19:24.400
Turn the other fucking cheek?

19:24.960 --> 19:28.200
We'll be handing out Bibles
in the fucking bullring with her cousins.

19:28.280 --> 19:32.040
John, you don't have to do anything.
Lizzie will do it for you.

19:32.120 --> 19:35.600
Then it'll all calm down,
and nobody will lose face.

19:35.680 --> 19:37.400
I'll take his fucking face.
How about that?

19:37.480 --> 19:39.200
-[door slams]
-John, do nothing... [sighing]

19:48.280 --> 19:50.880
I believe you have a reservation
for a private room

19:50.960 --> 19:52.360
in the name of Mr. Romanov.

19:55.000 --> 19:56.240
[clicks tongue]

19:56.320 --> 19:57.760
You work for Mr. Romanov?

19:59.360 --> 20:01.640
-Yes.
-For his household or his office?

20:02.040 --> 20:03.640
[sighing] Is there a problem?

20:03.720 --> 20:05.880
I'm afraid without the presence
of the Duke Mikhail Michailovich

20:05.960 --> 20:11.720
or Lady Lewington, we shall have to ask
for payment in advance.

20:12.560 --> 20:13.560
Can I ask why?

20:14.040 --> 20:17.160
Already, Mr. Romanov
has four outstanding bills with us.

20:17.640 --> 20:19.680
One for accommodation
and three for dining.

20:19.880 --> 20:22.840
And two banquets, which we wrote off.

20:23.040 --> 20:26.400
We've been asked to be understanding
of our Russian friends by His Majesty.

20:26.480 --> 20:28.760
-But it has been some time now...
-[thuds]

20:32.400 --> 20:34.360
-May I ask your name, sir?
-Shelby.

20:35.600 --> 20:38.560
Thomas Shelby, and in the future
I will be dining here quite a bit.

20:39.080 --> 20:41.760
-Then I shall put you on our special list.
-You do that.

20:43.000 --> 20:44.400
Here is a menu.

20:45.200 --> 20:47.360
I recommend the teal and the pork.

20:48.320 --> 20:50.880
Although your guest, I'm sure,
will order the caviar.

20:51.200 --> 20:53.800
[Leon] Myself and my wife and my niece
traveled by train,

20:53.880 --> 20:58.160
then coach, then on foot
through the Villa Ai-Todor in Crimea.

20:58.240 --> 21:00.800
On that journey I lost a toe.

21:01.400 --> 21:05.000
I don't know, I woke up one morning
and it was gone.

21:05.240 --> 21:07.520
All of a sudden I saw a dog,
and it was eating it.

21:08.520 --> 21:10.360
They said the British
had taken pity on us,

21:10.440 --> 21:12.520
and we were taken aboard HMS Marlborough.

21:13.120 --> 21:16.040
I immediately kissed the steel deck,
my lips froze to it.

21:16.320 --> 21:19.800
And then, of course, I thanked God
and your King for saving us.

21:21.200 --> 21:23.800
Though since then,
he has done nothing but humiliate me.

21:25.480 --> 21:27.840
Who? God or the King?

21:27.960 --> 21:29.400
Sometimes both, Mr. Shelby.

21:31.400 --> 21:34.600
Mmm, so, you met my niece already?

21:36.160 --> 21:37.800
Tatiana.

21:38.680 --> 21:40.880
Are you in love with her yet, hmm?

21:42.160 --> 21:45.640
You would be wise
not to love Russian women, you know.

21:45.920 --> 21:47.640
Ah, better not speak of Russian women.

21:47.720 --> 21:50.600
Mmm... That is the worst thing
about being here.

21:51.080 --> 21:53.600
Russian women, they know how to hold it

21:54.120 --> 21:57.720
and most important,
they know exactly when to let it go.

21:58.800 --> 22:00.520
Your cock, I mean.

22:02.040 --> 22:04.760
English women, they do not know so much.
You know?

22:09.320 --> 22:11.600
Did he die well, the spy?

22:14.240 --> 22:15.720
He begged for his life.

22:18.560 --> 22:20.560
I heard you had your brother do it.

22:24.200 --> 22:27.240
So you trust your family, like me,

22:28.720 --> 22:30.560
like us, Mr. Shelby.

22:32.840 --> 22:35.280
Let's talk about trust then, shall we?

22:37.240 --> 22:41.160
You are not a direct relation
to the Romanovs, you are Georgian.

22:41.240 --> 22:42.400
[glass shatters]

22:49.000 --> 22:51.360
And the palace where you live
in Hampton Court

22:51.560 --> 22:53.320
is, in fact, a grace and favor house

22:53.400 --> 22:56.880
donated to you, rent-free
by the British Crown.

22:57.080 --> 23:01.000
The maître d' here, tells me
that you are in some debt.

23:01.720 --> 23:04.040
Both here and other places, I imagine.

23:04.840 --> 23:09.120
See, I've been given ten,
but I've been promised 40.

23:11.280 --> 23:16.520
Already, I have had to have a man killed,
that sort of work does not come cheap.

23:17.360 --> 23:18.720
Do you understand?

23:44.640 --> 23:46.720
Let me tell you something, Mr. Shelby.

23:49.160 --> 23:50.720
Before we boarded the ship,

23:50.800 --> 23:54.560
my niece sewed 16 diamonds
into her velvet dress,

23:54.640 --> 23:58.720
and also she had two sapphires
in her intimate places.

24:00.120 --> 24:04.240
My wife managed two sapphires
and five diamonds.

24:05.200 --> 24:08.680
This is already for the killing of the spy

24:09.240 --> 24:11.960
and a down payment on future services.

24:15.280 --> 24:17.640
Now, tell me,
where do you keep these things?

24:17.760 --> 24:19.040
In a bank?

24:19.840 --> 24:22.320
How could we plead poverty
around London society

24:22.400 --> 24:24.800
if we used banks, Mr. Shelby?

24:26.680 --> 24:28.560
Well, you should know...

24:29.600 --> 24:32.280
Hatton Gardens is not safe.

24:33.560 --> 24:35.600
That's why we have our own treasury.

24:38.960 --> 24:42.720
Very well, I shall have
my people check its veracity.

24:44.600 --> 24:45.760
[Tommy grunts softly]

24:48.160 --> 24:52.440
Before the revolution began,
we were soft and weak.

24:53.240 --> 24:54.560
We made compromise.

24:55.480 --> 24:57.000
But let me tell you.

24:58.080 --> 25:01.000
We will never be soft and weak again.

25:01.760 --> 25:03.320
Do you understand?

25:06.800 --> 25:08.080
Good day, Mr. Shelby.

25:29.160 --> 25:31.120
[man] This way, Mr. Changretta.

25:31.560 --> 25:33.320
[man speaking Cantonese]

25:34.160 --> 25:36.040
Just there, sir. There.

25:38.400 --> 25:40.000
[yelling in Cantonese]

25:46.280 --> 25:48.280
["Crying Lightning" playing]

26:04.040 --> 26:05.360
[squelching]

26:12.280 --> 26:13.760
[Angel] Are you going to kill me?

26:14.360 --> 26:16.240
[John] Get fucking up.

26:16.320 --> 26:17.760
Stay away from Lizzie!

26:18.280 --> 26:19.960
[breathing heavily]

26:23.360 --> 26:25.160
-[slicing]
-[Angel groaning]

26:26.640 --> 26:28.080
[screaming]

26:28.840 --> 26:32.880
By order of the Peaky fucking Blinders!

26:32.960 --> 26:34.200
[Angel continues screaming]

26:48.480 --> 26:50.080
[Tommy] Going to introduce me, Michael?

26:50.760 --> 26:54.000
This is Charlotte Murray,
her father makes cars.

26:56.520 --> 26:58.720
I really enjoyed your wedding, Mr. Shelby.

27:00.720 --> 27:03.680
Polly said that you should call her.
There's been some trouble.

27:03.800 --> 27:05.080
[Tommy] What trouble?

27:06.800 --> 27:09.560
I'm guessing it's stuff
she doesn't like to tell me about.

27:11.760 --> 27:12.960
[Tommy] Nice to meet you.

27:19.080 --> 27:20.400
[chuckling]

27:29.200 --> 27:31.560
[Arthur] All right, Finn,
thanks for coming. Fuck off.

27:33.200 --> 27:35.160
Finn, you can stay.

27:38.280 --> 27:39.560
[inhales sharply] Sit down, John.

27:40.320 --> 27:41.520
Sit down.

27:47.760 --> 27:49.680
John, you cut Angel Changretta.

27:51.680 --> 27:54.680
-Even though Arthur told you to apologize.
-[John] Mmm-hmm.

27:55.240 --> 27:57.480
-[Tommy] Polly told you to compromise.
-[John] Mmm-hmm.

27:57.960 --> 28:01.280
You chose not to listen to Mr. Apologize
or Mrs. Compromise.

28:03.080 --> 28:05.760
And now I have got an Italian
walking around my backyard

28:05.880 --> 28:07.840
saying he's going to kill my brother.

28:09.640 --> 28:12.800
So what do we do, John.
Do we apologize or do we compromise?

28:20.080 --> 28:22.720
Oh, it was just something
John said as a joke.

28:24.280 --> 28:26.000
Yeah, but he's your brother
as well, Arthur.

28:26.560 --> 28:27.760
Yeah.

28:28.440 --> 28:29.960
I know I didn't want to start a war

28:30.040 --> 28:32.160
over something John said
without meaning it.

28:36.200 --> 28:39.760
So, should he apologize in Italian
or in English?

28:43.320 --> 28:46.000
Or should we ask them
which fucking language they prefer?

28:46.600 --> 28:47.720
I'm not clear.

28:51.000 --> 28:54.040
You said while this business was going on
in London, you wanted peace at home.

28:54.120 --> 28:55.680
And the only way to guarantee peace

28:55.760 --> 28:58.680
is by making the prospect of war
seem hopeless.

28:59.240 --> 29:03.400
If you apologize once,
you do it again and again and again.

29:03.520 --> 29:05.920
Like taking bricks out of the wall
of your fucking house.

29:06.120 --> 29:07.640
Do you want
to bring the house down, Arthur?

29:07.720 --> 29:10.720
-[Arthur grunts]
-If you're soft on rebellion, it'll grow.

29:10.800 --> 29:12.720
Bloody "soft on rebellion."

29:12.800 --> 29:14.680
You did the right thing, John.

29:14.760 --> 29:16.040
Now, we go on the offensive.

29:16.120 --> 29:19.400
We take two of the Changretta pubs,
and we take them tonight. That's it.

29:19.480 --> 29:21.760
Oh! Right. For Christ's sake, why?

29:21.840 --> 29:23.000
-Hey.
-Why?

29:23.080 --> 29:24.920
[Tommy] Why? Because we fucking can.

29:25.200 --> 29:28.360
Because we fucking can
and if we can, we do.

29:28.680 --> 29:32.520
And if we lift our heel off their necks
now, they'll just come at us.

29:34.640 --> 29:38.480
Remember these are the bastards
that wanted Danny Whizz-Bang dead.

29:44.000 --> 29:45.480
You're getting soft, brother.

29:45.600 --> 29:46.960
Soft and weak.

29:47.600 --> 29:49.720
Save the Bible for Sundays, eh.

29:53.960 --> 29:55.080
Finn?

29:55.680 --> 29:58.080
I need to get to Hockley and then home.

29:58.160 --> 29:59.960
It's been a long day.

30:04.040 --> 30:07.400
You take the Wrexham,
you take the Five Bells.

30:07.480 --> 30:10.240
You get them signed over to us
in the morning.

30:10.320 --> 30:11.960
You make sure the coppers stay away.

30:14.560 --> 30:18.440
Don't use the fucking phones, all right?
There's someone listening.

30:27.080 --> 30:28.400
[Arthur] Well done.

30:35.040 --> 30:36.680
[Polly slurping]

30:51.760 --> 30:53.440
[ringing]

31:00.520 --> 31:01.640
[conversing in Russian]

31:01.720 --> 31:03.480
These are all to be typed tonight,

31:03.560 --> 31:09.040
signed by you
and sent first post tomorrow.

31:10.200 --> 31:14.960
This is to Duke Michail Michailovich

31:15.160 --> 31:17.720
asking after his health

31:17.800 --> 31:21.480
and suggesting
an alternative date for lunch.

31:22.040 --> 31:24.800
This one is to Lady Lewington.

31:25.000 --> 31:26.640
It is quite flirtatious

31:27.560 --> 31:28.920
but I hear she is a whore

31:29.520 --> 31:33.280
and will respond.

31:33.360 --> 31:35.520
And this is to Mr. Shelby.

31:36.000 --> 31:39.920
He has the effrontery
to check our sapphires,

31:40.000 --> 31:45.200
we need proof
he has the material we require.

31:45.280 --> 31:48.480
At a time of our choosing.

31:51.320 --> 31:52.960
How much did you drink?

31:53.760 --> 31:56.000
Wine, no vodka.

31:56.800 --> 31:58.160
Hmm.

31:59.640 --> 32:03.880
At the end of this business

32:03.960 --> 32:09.880
you may have to kill Mr. Shelby yourself.

32:09.960 --> 32:11.000
Can you do it?

32:15.200 --> 32:16.640
Of course.

32:18.160 --> 32:19.560
[wind howling]

32:22.360 --> 32:24.920
[music playing over recorder]

32:25.000 --> 32:26.680
Not hungry, Mrs. Shelby?

32:26.800 --> 32:30.040
"Hungry"? Oh, no, sorry, Mary.

32:30.920 --> 32:32.320
You'll ruin your eyes.

32:36.320 --> 32:37.320
Tommy...

32:46.480 --> 32:48.240
-[Tommy] Hello.
-Hello.

32:50.520 --> 32:52.400
-Sit down.
-[clears throat]

32:57.000 --> 32:59.040
-Guess.
-Guess what?

33:04.240 --> 33:05.960
-He said yes.
-Who?

33:06.760 --> 33:10.560
The leader of the Birmingham City Council
is going to attend the dinner.

33:12.600 --> 33:15.800
-Everyone has said yes. Everyone.
-Ah. [clears throat]

33:15.880 --> 33:18.080
I keep having to change the catering.

33:19.320 --> 33:21.600
And my writing hand is almost falling off.

33:21.840 --> 33:23.720
Oh, what are you writing for?
I bought you a typewriter.

33:24.000 --> 33:27.600
[chuckles] You don't write letters
of a social occasion on a typewriter.

33:27.680 --> 33:30.120
-Oh. Forgive me.
-[chuckles]

33:32.200 --> 33:35.000
I have the drawings

33:35.080 --> 33:37.880
of what they plan to do
with the grounds of the house.

33:37.960 --> 33:40.560
There'll be an area
for the children to play. Look.

33:40.640 --> 33:41.760
Mmm-hmm.

33:41.840 --> 33:44.200
And the Birmingham Charity Commission
have agreed to set aside

33:44.280 --> 33:48.800
their three rotten floorboards upstairs
and grant us the license within a month.

33:52.240 --> 33:55.600
-You're not listening to me.
-Yes, I am. I am.

33:56.000 --> 33:58.480
Do you think I'm becoming obsessed?

33:59.560 --> 34:00.560
Yes.

34:02.040 --> 34:04.400
Should I ask you how your day was,
like a good wife?

34:05.040 --> 34:06.040
No.

34:09.000 --> 34:12.199
I'm guessing that means your day
was not as successful as mine, hmm.

34:12.719 --> 34:15.600
That all depends
on how you measure success.

34:16.920 --> 34:19.080
See, personally,

34:20.440 --> 34:21.800
I measure it in sapphires.

34:22.199 --> 34:23.560
[chuckling] Oh!

34:24.239 --> 34:26.560
-Sapphires. Mmm.
-Uh-huh.

34:28.880 --> 34:30.480
Close your eyes.

34:31.280 --> 34:32.600
[chuckles softly]

34:33.520 --> 34:35.120
[whispers] Close your eyes.

34:51.600 --> 34:53.679
All right, you can open 'em.

34:55.639 --> 34:56.840
Where the hell did you get that?

34:59.480 --> 35:00.640
It's beautiful.

35:04.040 --> 35:06.120
You can wear it to the foundation dinner.

35:08.080 --> 35:10.680
Don't you think it's a bit much
for a charity dinner?

35:10.960 --> 35:12.160
Grace,

35:12.960 --> 35:14.760
this is fucking Birmingham.

35:15.840 --> 35:19.160
"Good taste" is for people
who can't afford sapphires.

35:19.240 --> 35:20.800
[chuckling]

35:20.880 --> 35:22.400
Oh, Mr. Shelby.

35:24.800 --> 35:26.520
[thunder rumbling]

35:51.240 --> 35:53.520
Did you wind the clock, Arthur?

35:56.560 --> 35:58.320
We should go to bed.

35:59.960 --> 36:01.640
[breathes deeply]

36:04.000 --> 36:05.400
I need to...

36:06.480 --> 36:08.120
I need to go out.

36:09.760 --> 36:11.840
Some business I need to do.

36:18.320 --> 36:19.640
"Business"?

36:25.800 --> 36:27.480
But you only just got in.

36:27.680 --> 36:28.680
I won't be long.

36:28.760 --> 36:30.120
[Linda] It's 10:00.

36:31.920 --> 36:33.240
It's pouring with rain.

36:34.960 --> 36:36.080
I'll go...

36:37.040 --> 36:38.720
I'll go and I'll come back.

36:39.520 --> 36:40.520
Arthur.

36:44.200 --> 36:46.920
Working in the dark is for the devil.

36:47.800 --> 36:49.280
We said.

36:50.080 --> 36:52.240
Start to do your work in the light.

36:53.840 --> 36:55.360
Your own light.

36:56.520 --> 36:58.160
Inside your head.

37:00.600 --> 37:02.360
It's just paperwork.

37:13.160 --> 37:16.680
I need you to clear your men
out of Nechells tonight.

37:20.280 --> 37:25.280
I thought you boys were a bit grand
for this sort of thing these days.

37:25.360 --> 37:26.440
Moss.

37:27.680 --> 37:31.080
Mind you, I think Tommy enjoys the sport.

37:34.640 --> 37:35.960
Something like that.

37:37.240 --> 37:38.720
Good night, Arthur.

37:38.800 --> 37:39.960
Night.

37:47.000 --> 37:49.000
["I Might Be Wrong" playing]

37:54.040 --> 37:56.000
[people screaming]

38:18.960 --> 38:20.280
[John] Arthur, what are you doing?

38:25.680 --> 38:26.920
Arthur?

38:29.960 --> 38:32.080
We're going to the Garrison.

38:32.160 --> 38:34.760
[Arthur] No. I'm going home, John.

38:37.560 --> 38:39.480
[John] Go and fuck yourself, Arthur.

38:40.680 --> 38:42.200
Yeah! Fuck off!

38:46.960 --> 38:48.800
[Angel screaming]

38:54.160 --> 38:55.280
[nurse shushing]

38:57.880 --> 38:58.960
[conversing in Italian]

38:59.040 --> 39:01.120
He will catch the train
from Naples to Paris

39:01.600 --> 39:03.160
and then the boat train to London.

39:09.240 --> 39:12.440
And he can be here by Sunday, yes?

39:12.560 --> 39:14.600
[Angel continues screaming]

39:19.760 --> 39:22.000
[gentle music playing]

39:30.960 --> 39:32.640
-[Tommy] Come here, Charlie.
-[Grace] Charlie.

39:34.880 --> 39:38.000
This big man and his brother
are going to make us a lot of money.

39:38.400 --> 39:39.640
Or lose us a lot of money.

39:39.760 --> 39:43.240
Who the hell cares
when they are such beautiful beasts, eh?

39:44.960 --> 39:47.400
[Charlie mumbling]

39:51.400 --> 39:53.200
[indistinct]

39:57.280 --> 39:58.440
Go on.

40:10.880 --> 40:12.400
[Esme moaning]

40:16.320 --> 40:18.800
-[Tommy] You've got a house, John.
-[John] Oh, fuck.

40:21.080 --> 40:22.080
Full of kids.

40:22.160 --> 40:23.800
[Tommy] Well, you've got a maid
to look after the kids.

40:23.880 --> 40:25.280
[John] Yeah, she listens.

40:28.600 --> 40:30.640
[Tommy] Have you done the odds
for tomorrow?

40:30.720 --> 40:32.840
Something urgent came up.

40:32.920 --> 40:35.240
[John] They get worse
when they're pregnant, Tom.

40:36.200 --> 40:37.200
John.

40:37.600 --> 40:40.680
Esme, I need you to leave now.
Go out the back door,

40:40.800 --> 40:42.040
and lock it after you.

40:44.560 --> 40:46.160
Come on, I left the office.

40:46.840 --> 40:49.600
There's two trucks full of coppers
out there, John.

40:50.520 --> 40:51.600
Where the fuck is Arthur?

40:51.760 --> 40:54.400
He goes home to the Madonna of Moseley
on the stroke of 5:00.

40:54.480 --> 40:57.280
-[Esme] You need to talk to him, Tom.
-Esme, please, go. Now.

40:57.400 --> 40:58.400
Please.

40:59.080 --> 41:00.480
This is very fucking unusual.

41:00.640 --> 41:01.760
So, call Moss.

41:01.880 --> 41:05.360
They're from out of town.
London, by the looks of their boots...

41:05.440 --> 41:08.040
-Since when are we scared of coppers, Tom?
-[gun clicking]

41:08.120 --> 41:09.360
-Since things changed, John.
-[Esme screaming]

41:10.960 --> 41:12.760
-[officer 1] Scotland Yard!
-[officer 2] Get down! Police!

41:12.840 --> 41:14.440
-[officer 1] Go on!
-[Tommy] John!

41:14.920 --> 41:16.720
[clamoring]

41:16.800 --> 41:18.760
John! John, it's the Yard.

41:19.480 --> 41:21.360
-Put it down.
-Putting it down. Putting it fucking down.

41:21.440 --> 41:23.880
-Hands on your heads!
-Down on your knees! Now!

41:24.520 --> 41:26.800
Let her fucking go!
She's fucking pregnant.

41:27.760 --> 41:28.920
Leave her alone.

41:29.000 --> 41:30.440
What the fuck is happening, Tom?

41:30.520 --> 41:32.640
-[officer 1] Let's go.
-[Esme screams]

41:33.040 --> 41:34.240
[Esme] Put me down!

41:34.320 --> 41:37.600
-Tell Polly it's Russian business, John.
-All right.

41:37.680 --> 41:40.400
Peaky fucking Blinders my arse.

41:43.520 --> 41:46.120
-[Hughes] Is he afraid?
-No.

41:50.800 --> 41:52.360
Go on.

41:57.120 --> 41:58.200
Sit.

42:01.680 --> 42:03.920
I'm talking to you, Mr. Shelby.

42:06.120 --> 42:07.240
[scoffs]

42:16.360 --> 42:19.240
So, the Odd Fellows want you to know
that any deviation

42:19.320 --> 42:22.200
from your instructions
will have consequences.

42:22.760 --> 42:23.920
What's your dog's name?

42:26.240 --> 42:27.600
You visited your sister.

42:28.080 --> 42:29.880
Eh? What's your name, boy?

42:30.000 --> 42:31.640
[snarling]

42:32.400 --> 42:35.120
Your sister is a potential
security breach.

42:36.040 --> 42:38.840
She has connections
with the Bolsheviks in London

42:39.320 --> 42:41.320
who have connections
with the Soviet Embassy.

42:41.440 --> 42:43.360
I think I will just call your dog, "Boy."

42:45.280 --> 42:47.600
You love your Boy, don't you?

42:50.200 --> 42:51.640
Understand this.

42:52.960 --> 42:55.760
You have the local police in your pocket,

42:56.080 --> 42:57.920
we have Scotland Yard.

42:59.320 --> 43:02.280
They do what we tell them
just as surely as this dog...

43:03.440 --> 43:04.480
Let him off the leash.

43:07.040 --> 43:08.800
Are you hearing me, Mr. Shelby?

43:09.560 --> 43:11.520
I can charm dogs.

43:12.560 --> 43:14.200
Gypsy witchcraft.

43:15.240 --> 43:18.680
And those I can't charm,
I can kill with my own hands.

43:21.160 --> 43:23.320
You learn it
when you have a dog on a boat.

43:23.400 --> 43:25.680
They go fucking mad in tunnels.

43:27.000 --> 43:29.200
I feel like I'm in a tunnel now.

43:30.800 --> 43:34.480
You know that feeling,
when you have to kill or be killed?

43:39.560 --> 43:41.000
Let the dog off the leash

43:41.880 --> 43:44.120
and give the order you give in Gaelic...

43:45.720 --> 43:46.880
Like I'm told you do

43:46.960 --> 43:50.560
when someone displeases you
or someone reports you.

43:51.640 --> 43:55.080
Visit your sister again,
and she will die crossing the road.

43:58.160 --> 43:59.080
[in Gaelic]
Kill!

44:02.840 --> 44:04.280
[in English] Then you say it.

44:10.440 --> 44:13.280
If you wanted me dead,
I would be dead, wouldn't I?

44:13.440 --> 44:14.800
[scoffs]

44:16.320 --> 44:17.680
It's true.

44:18.760 --> 44:20.560
It's true, we do need you alive.

44:22.160 --> 44:24.080
But when you go home today, Mr. Shelby...

44:25.720 --> 44:28.280
Be sure to check
under your little boy's pillow.

44:29.360 --> 44:31.360
The tooth fairy has been.

44:34.200 --> 44:35.960
We can reach anyone.

44:36.480 --> 44:37.720
Anywhere.

44:39.800 --> 44:41.080
[knocking]

44:44.480 --> 44:46.440
[rock music playing]

45:07.680 --> 45:09.000
[Charlie crying]

45:18.160 --> 45:20.480
-Is everything all right?
-[panting] Yes.

45:20.960 --> 45:22.680
Everything's fine. Everything's fine.

45:23.320 --> 45:24.320
Yeah.

45:24.680 --> 45:26.880
You promised, Tommy.

45:26.960 --> 45:28.520
[breathing heavily]

45:28.600 --> 45:30.400
I trust you.

45:33.280 --> 45:34.960
-I trust you, Tommy.
-Yes.

45:37.760 --> 45:40.560
[softly] He's fine. He's fine.

45:41.760 --> 45:43.520
[Charlie crying]

45:50.880 --> 45:52.920
Grace. Grace.

45:54.000 --> 45:55.560
[whispering] We gotta go.

46:09.440 --> 46:11.240
You're not one of those
Impressionists, are you?

46:11.360 --> 46:13.040
They're all terribly political,
aren't they?

46:14.200 --> 46:15.960
-And you're not?
-Goodness no.

46:16.600 --> 46:19.720
The people I work for just
want me to paint what is there.

46:19.800 --> 46:22.440
To me, politics is deliberately
making things better

46:22.520 --> 46:25.240
for some people by deliberately
making them worse for others.

46:25.320 --> 46:26.440
[footsteps approaching]

46:32.720 --> 46:34.120
Well, I thought I might wear this.

46:38.320 --> 46:40.360
Oh, God. It's too much.
I'll try something more simple.

46:40.480 --> 46:42.160
No. Don't...

46:44.240 --> 46:46.080
Suddenly, I feel incompetent.

46:47.160 --> 46:50.160
I want the portrait to hang in the office,
so I want it to look formal.

46:50.240 --> 46:51.840
[Ruben] It's not formal.

46:52.680 --> 46:53.720
It's beautiful.

46:56.160 --> 46:57.240
It was made in Paris.

46:58.000 --> 46:59.560
It was stolen in Birmingham.
[chuckles nervously]

46:59.920 --> 47:03.400
My mother stole it from a house
she was cleaning. 1901.

47:03.480 --> 47:04.880
[Ruben] No. No.

47:04.960 --> 47:06.720
It's yours. It belongs on you.

47:08.000 --> 47:10.200
A woman of substance and class.

47:10.280 --> 47:12.320
Believe me. I've painted many women

47:12.400 --> 47:14.480
who don't belong
in their expensive dresses.

47:16.720 --> 47:17.960
There'll be no charge.

47:18.640 --> 47:20.280
Your normal rate.

47:20.720 --> 47:22.880
-I insist.
-Hmm! There's a first.

47:25.280 --> 47:27.880
-So, when shall we start?
-I've already started.

47:28.960 --> 47:30.720
Come to my studio this evening.

47:30.840 --> 47:33.320
-[Polly] Uh, I am busy this evening.
-Polly, invite him.

47:34.280 --> 47:35.320
Invite me to what?

47:35.400 --> 47:37.480
Ada, this is a professional transaction.

47:37.560 --> 47:40.000
-Invite me to what?
-[Ada] Shelby Foundation dinner.

47:40.080 --> 47:42.200
-Polly's going alone. You're invited...
-[Polly] Ada.

47:45.760 --> 47:48.240
I'll come to your studio on Sunday.

47:49.240 --> 47:51.200
And then we shall begin.

47:57.080 --> 47:59.080
["This Is Love" playing]

48:03.600 --> 48:07.360
♪ You're the only story
That I never told ♪

48:07.440 --> 48:12.000
♪ You're my dirty little secret
Want to keep you so ♪

48:12.080 --> 48:15.800
♪ You're the only story
That never been told ♪

48:15.880 --> 48:20.520
♪ You're my dirty little secret
Want to keep you so ♪

48:20.600 --> 48:24.440
♪ Come on out, come on over
Help me forget ♪

48:24.520 --> 48:29.040
♪ Keep the walls from falling
As they're tumbling in ♪

48:29.120 --> 48:33.240
♪ Come on out, come on over
Help me forget ♪

48:33.320 --> 48:37.840
♪ Keep the walls from falling on me
Tumbling in ♪

48:37.920 --> 48:41.520
♪ Keep the walls from falling
As they're tumbling in ♪

48:42.080 --> 48:44.240
[indistinct conversations]

48:45.880 --> 48:49.800
♪ This is love
This is love that I'm feeling ♪

48:49.880 --> 48:53.040
♪ This is love... ♪

48:53.120 --> 48:54.880
A woman of substance...

48:56.920 --> 48:58.240
...and class.

49:06.480 --> 49:08.560
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

49:15.880 --> 49:16.880
Hello.

49:18.600 --> 49:19.600
[woman] Hello, Polly.

49:27.840 --> 49:30.240
[indistinct]

49:35.880 --> 49:37.080
Tommy.

49:39.120 --> 49:40.960
He's the leader
of the Birmingham City Council.

49:41.520 --> 49:42.840
-Hello, Tommy.
-Hi, Danny.

49:42.920 --> 49:44.240
[Daniel] How's the business?

49:44.320 --> 49:46.440
[Tommy] All right, it's holding up,
holding up. How are you?

49:46.960 --> 49:48.080
You know each other?

49:48.800 --> 49:51.880
[Daniel chuckles] I have interests
in a steelworks in Cradley Heath.

49:51.960 --> 49:55.480
Tommy helps me get my products
to the carmakers.

49:55.680 --> 49:58.400
Congratulations, Mrs. Shelby,
on your wedding.

49:58.480 --> 50:00.680
Thank you,
I'm surprised you weren't invited.

50:00.760 --> 50:02.680
Now, how would that look, eh?

50:04.360 --> 50:07.240
Oh, now, the party has really started.

50:07.320 --> 50:08.480
Who are they?

50:08.640 --> 50:12.360
[Daniel] Father John Hughes
from St. Mary's Boys Reformatory.

50:12.440 --> 50:15.640
And with him is Mr. Patrick Jarvis, MP.

50:15.720 --> 50:20.560
They are part of an organization
called the Economic League.

50:20.640 --> 50:22.360
Did you invite them, Grace?

50:22.560 --> 50:24.040
Their names sound familiar.

50:24.920 --> 50:26.760
They were recommended by the Lord Mayor.

50:26.840 --> 50:30.040
Oh. On your
"best people of the city" list, eh?

50:30.240 --> 50:32.600
-[Grace] Do you know them?
-I'll introduce you, Tommy.

50:32.680 --> 50:36.080
That's all right, Danny.
I'll introduce myself.

50:50.320 --> 50:52.760
We appear to have taken you by surprise.

50:53.280 --> 50:54.920
I have adjusted.

50:56.520 --> 50:58.800
Since the socialists
got into Downing Street

50:58.880 --> 51:00.080
we are all being followed.

51:00.160 --> 51:02.440
We have to meet in places
where we'd meet anyway.

51:02.520 --> 51:03.840
You should have stopped by Small Heath.

51:03.920 --> 51:05.800
I could have given you
a more traditional welcome.

51:05.880 --> 51:09.400
-They want to know about ammunition.
-[Patrick] And chains for the wheels.

51:09.480 --> 51:11.960
When the White Guard
make their run for Tbilisi,

51:12.040 --> 51:13.640
it will be over rough terrain.

51:13.880 --> 51:17.400
[inhales sharply] The chains are suitable
for snow or wet ground.

51:17.480 --> 51:19.280
They're already stowed on the vehicles.

51:19.360 --> 51:21.240
There's a batch of weapons
set aside at the BSA,

51:21.320 --> 51:23.080
which is bound for the Turkish army.

51:23.400 --> 51:25.680
And how will you get it all aboard
the London train?

51:25.760 --> 51:27.920
There will be a strike that night
across the city.

51:28.760 --> 51:31.240
You will have to stop
the train twice. How?

51:32.120 --> 51:35.000
Two drivers will join the strike
at different points.

51:36.720 --> 51:42.000
Rather fun, getting the Communist unions
to help get weapons to the Whites.

51:42.080 --> 51:43.520
[Tommy] Yes, rather fun, eh?

51:44.960 --> 51:47.120
I am thinking ahead,
thinking of every possibility,

51:47.200 --> 51:49.000
remembering everything that is happening.

51:49.120 --> 51:50.280
[Patrick scoffs]

51:52.000 --> 51:54.320
The Russians want to inspect the vehicles.

51:55.800 --> 51:58.120
-I'll take photographs.
-[Patrick] Mmm-mmm.

51:58.200 --> 52:01.240
The Duke has sent his niece, she's here.

52:02.160 --> 52:04.880
Tomorrow you will take her to the factory
and show her.

52:04.960 --> 52:08.640
No. Union conveners
are watching the factories.

52:10.520 --> 52:11.560
Not possible.

52:12.840 --> 52:15.960
Anything is possible, Mr. Shelby.

52:16.040 --> 52:17.720
You will take her.

52:18.680 --> 52:21.080
You will pick her up
from this hotel at 10:00.

52:22.600 --> 52:25.400
Now, look, a priest with an empty glass.

52:26.760 --> 52:28.920
Let's get back to the party.

52:30.880 --> 52:35.920
You know, gentlemen, there is hell
and there is another place below hell.

52:37.720 --> 52:39.760
I will remember everything...

52:40.680 --> 52:42.400
and forget nothing.

52:47.080 --> 52:49.040
[indistinct conversations]

52:52.080 --> 52:53.280
[Grace] Tommy,

52:53.360 --> 52:55.640
this is Duchess Tatiana Petrovna.

52:55.800 --> 52:57.120
[clears throat]

52:57.200 --> 52:59.320
Come on, Tommy, aren't you impressed
to meet a real duchess?

52:59.560 --> 53:01.480
Well, I understand they charge a fee.

53:01.720 --> 53:04.480
[scoffs] Mr. Shelby, you are very direct.

53:04.560 --> 53:05.840
Too direct.

53:05.920 --> 53:07.120
[Tatiana chuckles] But it's true.

53:07.760 --> 53:10.040
I attend these things for the champagne.

53:10.240 --> 53:12.640
And for the chance
to be treated like a duchess again.

53:13.000 --> 53:15.600
You should have kissed my hand,
Mr. Shelby.

53:17.920 --> 53:19.280
Forgive me.

53:21.720 --> 53:23.480
She was asking about my sapphire.

53:23.560 --> 53:26.560
-I thought I recognized it.
-She said it was Russian.

53:26.640 --> 53:29.520
My husband has business in Russia.
Perhaps you know about it, Tatiana?

53:29.600 --> 53:31.400
Well, tonight is not a night
for business, eh?

53:31.480 --> 53:33.400
Is that why you were in the concert hall
for ten minutes?

53:33.480 --> 53:34.800
I think people are ready
for dinner now, Grace.

53:35.000 --> 53:37.000
No, no. I'm not done
pumping people for money.

53:37.280 --> 53:38.680
What is "pump for money"?

53:38.840 --> 53:40.680
It's what I do every day.

53:41.480 --> 53:43.160
You know each other, do you?

53:44.120 --> 53:46.160
You see, I am in charge
of compiling the list of guests,

53:46.240 --> 53:48.520
but it's my husband
who seems to know all of them.

53:48.600 --> 53:50.040
I hear he is very well connected.

53:50.120 --> 53:52.040
And where does a duchess hear that?

53:52.240 --> 53:53.280
In certain circles.

53:53.360 --> 53:54.560
All right, enough. Ada.

53:54.720 --> 53:56.280
Grace, there's a Lady Dowager

53:56.360 --> 53:58.400
who wants to speak to you
about coffee mornings.

53:58.480 --> 54:00.720
She mentioned a £2,000 cash donation.

54:00.880 --> 54:03.000
Tatiana, you and I will speak later.

54:03.080 --> 54:04.600
[Tatiana] I would like that.

54:06.840 --> 54:09.000
Going to the factory tomorrow
is a mistake.

54:10.040 --> 54:11.720
Nevertheless, we will go.

54:13.120 --> 54:16.440
Also, my uncle ordered me to seduce you
to give us an advantage.

54:16.520 --> 54:19.040
But with a beautiful wife like that
it will be difficult, no?

54:19.120 --> 54:20.560
Tomorrow is a mistake.

54:20.960 --> 54:23.400
Have you not heard?
We have no morals, we Russians.

54:23.640 --> 54:24.640
And no fucking sense.

54:24.720 --> 54:26.320
And no options.

54:26.800 --> 54:30.040
I would fuck you for the cause.
What do you think of that?

54:31.040 --> 54:33.080
I think you should not drink
vodka with champagne.

54:34.720 --> 54:37.080
[Tatiana] Does your wife know
that the sapphire she is wearing

54:37.160 --> 54:39.200
has been cursed by a Gypsy?

54:40.200 --> 54:41.760
[chuckling]

54:43.400 --> 54:44.320
What did you say?

54:44.800 --> 54:47.920
Nothing on Earth would make me wear it.

55:02.760 --> 55:04.920
Grace, listen to me. Look, I can explain.

55:05.120 --> 55:06.120
-Go away.
-It's...

55:06.200 --> 55:07.400
[MC] Ladies and gentlemen.

55:07.480 --> 55:08.640
For once, you shouldn't have to explain.

55:08.720 --> 55:12.080
The loyalty toast,
to His Majesty the King.

55:12.200 --> 55:13.960
[all] To the King.

55:14.360 --> 55:15.880
[MC] Dinner is served.

55:16.080 --> 55:18.120
[Tommy] You look beautiful,
but you need to take this off.

55:18.200 --> 55:19.760
Why? Because you think
it would look better on her?

55:19.840 --> 55:22.560
Grace, look at me, fuck these people, eh.

55:22.640 --> 55:25.720
Fuck 'em, I need you to be all right.

55:26.040 --> 55:29.520
I need you, Grace. I need you.

55:36.840 --> 55:39.080
Damn you, Tommy Shelby. [chuckles]

55:50.440 --> 55:51.920
[chuckles]

55:52.000 --> 55:53.520
-Shall we go inside?
-Yeah.

55:56.560 --> 55:57.880
For Angel!

55:59.600 --> 56:00.760
[gunshot]

56:00.960 --> 56:02.880
[people screaming]

56:11.400 --> 56:14.640
Get me a fucking ambulance now!

56:57.400 --> 56:59.400
[theme song playing]

57:12.960 --> 57:15.800
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

57:15.880 --> 57:17.760
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

57:17.840 --> 57:19.880
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

57:19.960 --> 57:22.160
♪ A red right hand ♪
